.SS "Uint8Array getBytes (uint start, uint len)"

.PP
Copy a bounded byte range into a plain Uint8Array\&. The requested length is clamped to the remaining bytes\&. An offset at or beyond the end returns an empty array\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstart\fP Zero-based byte offset\&. 
.br
\fIlen\fP Maximum number of bytes to copy\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A fresh, independently owned Uint8Array\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "Uint8Array getData ()"

.PP
Copy the block's bytes into a new plain Uint8Array\&. Returns the same standard JavaScript array type on desktop native, Node, browser, and iOS runtimes\&. Each call copies all bytes without text decoding, including zero and values above 127\&. Changing the returned array does not change this \fBMemBlock\fP or arrays returned by earlier calls\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independently owned Uint8Array with \fBgetDataSize()\fP elements, or an empty Uint8Array for an empty block\&. The result is not a Node Buffer; slice() copies bytes and subarray() shares the returned array's memory\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const writer = new pdg\&.Serializer();
writer\&.serialize_1u(255);
const bytes = writer\&.getDataPtr()\&.getData();
const copy = bytes\&.slice();

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBNode\&.js Buffer conversion\fP
.RS 4
Use this form when a Node\&.js API specifically requires a Buffer\&. \fBgetData()\fP copies the native block once; the Buffer then shares that snapshot without another payload copy\&. Include the offset and length so only the array's visible bytes are exposed, even when converting a subarray\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
These examples require Node\&.js Buffer support\&. The shared Buffer and Uint8Array reflect each other's mutations, but neither changes the \fBMemBlock\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const bytes = writer\&.getDataPtr()\&.getData();
const buffer = Buffer\&.from(bytes\&.buffer, bytes\&.byteOffset, bytes\&.byteLength);
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
The shorter form below makes an additional full copy of the bytes: one copy from native memory into the Uint8Array, then another into the Buffer\&. For an N-byte block, it copies 2N bytes and needs storage for both N-byte payloads until the temporary array can be collected\&. This adds copy time and memory/garbage-collection pressure, especially for large or frequent transfers\&. Use it when an independent Buffer copy is intentional\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const bufferCopy = Buffer\&.from(writer\&.getDataPtr()\&.getData());
.fi
.PP

.PP
The removed MemBlock\&.toBuffer() method can be replaced by the shared-view form above with the same single payload copy\&. 
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetBytes()\fP 
.RE
.PP

